:: WatchChildrenPlay [childhood]
# Games and Play

You approach the group of children playing near the center of camp. They are engaged in a game of chase, squealing with delight as they run between shelters. One of the older children, about six summers old, notices you watching.

"<<print $character.name>>! Come play with us!" she calls. Her name is <<if $language eq "proto-indo-european">>Saulā<<elseif $language eq "proto-uralic">>Aino<<else>>Nefert<</if>>, and she often looks out for the younger children.

The game is simple but teaches important skills - quick movements, dodging, and awareness of your surroundings. These same skills will be vital later in life for hunting or avoiding dangers.

As you play, you notice how the older children sometimes let the younger ones catch them, teaching through encouragement rather than competition.

<<link "Join the game of chase">>
  <<set $skills.running += 0.3>>
  <<set $relationships.bestFriend += 5>>
  <<goto "PlayChase">>
<</link>>

<<link "Watch a different game with sticks and stones">>
  <<set $skills.perception += 0.2>>
  <<goto "WatchSticksAndStones">>
<</link>>